   "id": "muster",
   "title": "Payday and a plan",
   "time": "7 September",
   "narrative": "On the morning of 7 September the army of Publius Quinctilius Varus mustered near its summer quarters west of the Weser, and the year's third pay was handed out. Word went round that plunder would be allowed on the coming expedition. Arminius, trusted by Varus, had urged a short cut through Angrivarian land to put down a revolt that he had himself invented. That evening he left the camp, saying he would gather his Cherusci and rejoin in a few days. He rode north to raise the Angrivarii and Bructeri. A few Cherusci stayed with the Romans as guides and spies.",
