   "id": "bructeri-raid",
   "title": "The column is struck along its length",
   "time": "Late morning, 8 September",
   "narrative": "The Roman column now ran for 15 to 20 kilometres through forest and mud. Bructeri warriors fell on it in many places, throwing javelins and then pulling away. This raid was meant to tire the men and bruise the baggage rather than destroy the army. Losses were light, but wagons and the scouting horse suffered most. The Roman column could not form a line in the trees.",
