   "id": "rain-camp",
   "title": "Rain and a camp in the forest",
   "time": "Afternoon, 8 September",
   "narrative": "A cloudburst turned the forest tracks to mud, and Varus ordered a halt. His men dug a camp and the commanders held a council. The reports showed modest losses, and the damage to the baggage was plain. The Germans withdrew into the trees. The exact position of this camp is unknown and is shown here in a reconstructed place. The army had been drawn off the paths it knew and into the territory chosen by Arminius.",
