  {
   "id": "pass",
   "title": "The gap at Kalkriese",
   "time": "Dawn, 9 September",
   "narrative": "The head of the column ran into a corridor barely 100 metres wide, between the wooded hill and the edge of the bog. A ditch crossed the road, and a zigzag wall of turf and packed sand ran along the hillside, hiding warriors who could throw down on the marching men. The column was stopped and bunched at the front while the rest of it, many kilometres behind, was still moving up. Arminius's plan was to catch it unable to deploy.",
