  {
   "id": "assault",
   "title": "The Roman attempt on the wall",
   "time": "Morning, 9 September",
   "narrative": "The legionaries tried to storm the wall, forming up as well as the narrow strip allowed. Finds in front of the line, and almost none behind it, show that they never broke through. Missiles fell on them from above. Germanic bands also struck the stalled column from the north and east, and the baggage train piled up behind. The fight turned into a slow butchery.",
