   "title": "The Romans are overrun",
   "time": "Afternoon, 9 September",
   "narrative": "Warriors came over the wall and across the bog edge and cut down the broken Roman formations. Varus took his own life, as did other officers, among them Ceionius, who had first given himself up. Eggius died fighting at the head of his men. Roman dead are estimated at 15,000 to 20,000. Some captives were sacrificed, according to Tacitus.",
