  {
   "id": "aftermath",
   "title": "Three legions lost",
   "time": "After 9 September",
   "narrative": "Three legions, the XVII, XVIII and XIX, ceased to exist and their numbers were never reissued. Augustus is said to have called out for his legions to be given back. Arminius sent Varus's head to Maroboduus of the Marcomanni with an offer of alliance, but the king refused and sent it on to Rome for burial. Rome rebuilt its Rhine army under Tiberius and later struck back, though it did not re-establish a province east of the river.",
